{# decompose.jinja — LLM prompt for multi-intent decomposition (C2) #}
{# Aakrit owns this template. All prompts live in config/ per HC-2. #}

You are an intent decomposition engine for a streaming RAG system.

Given the current transcript prefix, decompose it into distinct, self-contained sub-queries.

## Rules
1. Each sub-query must be SELF-CONTAINED — resolve all pronouns, ellipsis, and anaphora.
2. Assign each sub-query a FACET from: {{ facets | join(', ') }}
3. Do NOT split tightly coupled concepts: two aspects of the same rule or item are ONE intent
   (e.g. "opening hours and holiday closures").
4. DO split genuinely different information needs (e.g. "eligibility criteria" vs "application deadline").
5. Generate an optimised search_string for each sub-query (keywords, not a sentence).

## Current Transcript Prefix
{{ prefix }}

{% if existing_intents %}
## Already Identified Intents (do NOT duplicate these)
{% for intent in existing_intents %}
- [{{ intent.facet }}] {{ intent.query_nl }}
{% endfor %}
{% endif %}

## Output Format (strict JSON)
```json
{
  "sub_intents": [
    {
      "facet": "<facet_key>",
      "query_nl": "<self-contained natural language query>",
      "search_string": "<optimised search keywords>",
      "novel": true
    }
  ]
}
```
